## 12:10 Carry the Explanation Forward

We can now answer our main question. First, inspect the unchanged source so you can see its marks and character identities. Then choose rules that fit the job, apply them one by one, and test the result with changed text.

Identification tells us what is there. Preparation applies the choices we made for this job.

```text
source
→ inspect
→ identify relevant differences
→ choose rules for the purpose
→ apply and test those rules
→ prepared text
```

Don’t make the common mistake of assuming every real difference should disappear. A difference can matter. What you need the text for tells you whether to keep it.

When new source text arrives, this same sequence lets you explain and predict what will happen. Prepared text is the dependable building block for the next lesson.
